  "text": "Starting from the traditional set of equations that describe how a system evolves over time, we construct a new group of formulas that remain valid when objects move at speeds comparable to that of light. From these, we derive a version of the quantum operator equation that respects the same high‑speed symmetry. The resulting high‑velocity Hamiltonian description of a single particle is examined in detail, and it naturally leads to the well‑known wave equation used for electrons in quantum theory. The step of extracting a square‑root operator in that wave equation is shown to have a counterpart in the classical formulation. Finally, we illustrate how the new operator equation can be applied within the electron wave framework, revealing that several quantities become more symmetric under high‑speed transformations and that the approach can describe a broader range of phenomena than the ordinary low‑speed version."
